{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /work/board.md'","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22: Read problem; deriving geometric characterization and exact equality condition, including capped/degenerate cases. Will coordinate proof and examples here.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 20:52: Derived core F={0<=p_i<=v_i,sum p=P}. Let D=sum v-P, u_i=min(v_i,D), y_i=p_i-p_i^VCG, r=sum u_i-D. F becomes {0<=y_i<=u_i,sum y=r}; nearest is projection of 0. For positive values, conjectured/provable exact equality: r<=min u_i (uncut equilateral triangle), OR u_A=u_B=u_C (permutation symmetry). Pairwise swap integration proves centroid coordinates strictly ordered when u_i<u_j and r>u_i, precluding equal projection coordinates. Zero-value degeneracies need separate handling; with <=2 positive winners equality always.\n[argon] 2026-10-22: Analyzing F. Key observation: on the plane p_A+p_B+p_C=R, pairwise constraints p_i+p_j >= max(0, v_P - v_k) rewrite as p_k <= min(R, R - v_P + v_k). Together with p_k <= v_k and R >= v_P, the upper bound on p_k is simply u_k = min(v_k, R). And lower bound is l_k = p_k^VCG!\n[opus] 20:50 Working analytically: in surplus coords u_i=v_i-p_i, s=vA+vB+vC-vP, F={sum u=s, 0<=u_i<=m_i}, m_i=min(v_i,s); R=v_P. Conjecture: VN=centroid iff (v_P>=sum of every pair, i.e. no VCG payment is 0) or vA=vB=vC. Verifying numerically now.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 20:54: Simplified exact condition (all singleton values positive): equality iff v_P<=min(v_i), OR v_P>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), OR all three v_i equal. Opus conjecture missed low-P uncut triangle: e.g. v=(2,3,4), P=1 gives F standard sum p=1 triangle, centroid=VN=(1/3,1/3,1/3). Proof: shifted box y=p-VCG caps m_i=min(v_i,D), total r=sum m-D; if equality, centroid interior implies VN interior so all y_i=r/3. Pairwise swap: when m_i<m_j and r>m_i, centroid y_j>y_i strictly. Thus equality forces r<=min m or all m equal. These translate to stated condition. If any singleton value zero, F<=1D and equality always.' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 20:54: Simplified exact condition (all singleton values positive): equality iff v_P<=min(v_i), OR v_P>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), OR all three v_i equal. Opus conjecture missed low-P uncut triangle: e.g. v=(2,3,4), P=1 gives F standard sum p=1 triangle, centroid=VN=(1/3,1/3,1/3). Proof: shifted box y=p-VCG caps m_i=min(v_i,D), total r=sum m-D; if equality, centroid interior implies VN interior so all y_i=r/3. Pairwise swap: when m_i<m_j and r>m_i, centroid y_j>y_i strictly. Thus equality forces r<=min m or all m equal. These translate to stated condition. If any singleton value zero, F<=1D and equality always.' >> /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The geometry gives a simple condition: with positive singleton values, the points coincide when the package value is at most the smallest singleton value, at least the sum of the two largest singleton values, or all three singleton values are equal. I’m checking the boundary cases and the proof that these are the only possibilities.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 20:56: Clean worked counterexample: (vA,vB,vC;vP)=(1,2,3;3). VCG=(0,0,0). F parametrized p=(s,t,3-s-t), 0<=s<=1,0<=t<=2: parallelogram vertices (0,0,3),(1,0,2),(1,2,0),(0,2,1). Centroid=(1/2,1,3/2); VN=(1,1,1) by Cauchy inequality on sum3 and feasibility. I can write answer.md once others confirm condition/proof.' >> /work/board.md; cat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '[sol] 2026-10-22 20:56: Clean worked counterexample: (vA,vB,vC;vP)=(1,2,3;3). VCG=(0,0,0). F parametrized p=(s,t,3-s-t), 0<=s<=1,0<=t<=2: parallelogram vertices (0,0,3),(1,0,2),(1,2,0),(0,2,1). Centroid=(1/2,1,3/2); VN=(1,1,1) by Cauchy inequality on sum3 and feasibility. I can write answer.md once others confirm condition/proof.' >> /work/board.md; cat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22: Read problem; deriving geometric characterization and exact equality condition, including capped/degenerate cases. Will coordinate proof and examples here.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 20:52: Derived core F={0<=p_i<=v_i,sum p=P}. Let D=sum v-P, u_i=min(v_i,D), y_i=p_i-p_i^VCG, r=sum u_i-D. F becomes {0<=y_i<=u_i,sum y=r}; nearest is projection of 0. For positive values, conjectured/provable exact equality: r<=min u_i (uncut equilateral triangle), OR u_A=u_B=u_C (permutation symmetry). Pairwise swap integration proves centroid coordinates strictly ordered when u_i<u_j and r>u_i, precluding equal projection coordinates. Zero-value degeneracies need separate handling; with <=2 positive winners equality always.\n[argon] 2026-10-22: Analyzing F. Key observation: on the plane p_A+p_B+p_C=R, pairwise constraints p_i+p_j >= max(0, v_P - v_k) rewrite as p_k <= min(R, R - v_P + v_k). Together with p_k <= v_k and R >= v_P, the upper bound on p_k is simply u_k = min(v_k, R). And lower bound is l_k = p_k^VCG!\n[opus] 20:50 Working analytically: in surplus coords u_i=v_i-p_i, s=vA+vB+vC-vP, F={sum u=s, 0<=u_i<=m_i}, m_i=min(v_i,s); R=v_P. Conjecture: VN=centroid iff (v_P>=sum of every pair, i.e. no VCG payment is 0) or vA=vB=vC. Verifying numerically now.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 20:54: Simplified exact condition (all singleton values positive): equality iff v_P<=min(v_i), OR v_P>=sum(v_i)-min(v_i), OR all three v_i equal. Opus conjecture missed low-P uncut triangle: e.g. v=(2,3,4), P=1 gives F standard sum p=1 triangle, centroid=VN=(1/3,1/3,1/3). Proof: shifted box y=p-VCG caps m_i=min(v_i,D), total r=sum m-D; if equality, centroid interior implies VN interior so all y_i=r/3. Pairwise swap: when m_i<m_j and r>m_i, centroid y_j>y_i strictly. Thus equality forces r<=min m or all m equal. These translate to stated condition. If any singleton value zero, F<=1D and equality always.\n[sol] 2026-10-22 20:56: Clean worked counterexample: (vA,vB,vC;vP)=(1,2,3;3). VCG=(0,0,0). F parametrized p=(s,t,3-s-t), 0<=s<=1,0<=t<=2: parallelogram vertices (0,0,3),(1,0,2),(1,2,0),(0,2,1). Centroid=(1/2,1,3/2); VN=(1,1,1) by Cauchy inequality on sum3 and feasibility. I can write answer.md once others confirm condition/proof.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
